---
/*
 * Homepage. Order, and why:
 *   1 Hero            one promise
 *   2 The reframe     revenue and margin; applies to both buyers, so before the fork
 *   3 The fork        self-select in about four seconds
 *   4 The problem     the seat you need and cannot justify full-time
 *   5 How we work     the machine: the method run by the reader's scroll
 *   6 Ways to work    how the method is bought: one way in, two ways to continue
 *   7 Who you get     two named operators and their track record, above any
 *                     client proof, because they are the proof a method lacks
 *   8 Qualifier       capacity is limited; say so, then book
 *
 * Sections alternate ink and cream. How we work is ink: Andrew chose the
 * machine on black, where its red backlights read as real light. Copy is a
 * working draft, refined with Andrew and Tarren.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Machine from "../components/Machine.astro";
import MachineRun from "../components/MachineRun.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
import BioBlock from "../components/BioBlock.astro";
import Placeholder from "../components/Placeholder.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import heroPhoto from "../assets/hero/andrew-and-tarren.webp";
---

<Base
  title="Fractional CRO, CMO and GTM Leadership | The Growth Machine"
  description="Fractional CRO, CMO, GTM and ecommerce leadership from founders who judge growth by profit. We find your next revenue and what's leaking, then lead the work."
>
  <Hero
    label="Fractional CRO · CMO · GTM lead"
    title="More revenue. Better margins. Without the full-time hire."
    image={heroPhoto}
    imageAlt="Andrew and Tarren Price at a desk, working through something on a laptop together."
  >
    <p>
      Founders who've run businesses on our own money, so we judge growth by profit, not activity. We find your next
      revenue and what's leaking, then do the work or lead your team through it.
    </p>
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <Button href="/call">Book a 30-minute call</Button>
      <a class="link" href="#how-we-work">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <Section
    tone="cream"
    label="Both sides of the number"
    title="More revenue is only good news if more of it stays."
  >
    <div class="reframe">
      <Machine />
      <div class="sides">
        <div class="side">
          <h3 class="display h3">Revenue</h3>
          <p>New ways to earn, better ways to earn, and more from the same effort.</p>
          <p class="levers muted">Go-to-market · Pricing · Channels · Retention</p>
        </div>
        <div class="side">
          <h3 class="display h3">Margin</h3>
          <p>Money the business already makes and quietly loses on the way out.</p>
          <p class="levers muted">Fees and costs · Processes · Team shape · Wasted spend</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="measures">
      <div class="measure">
        <p class="label">A CMO</p>
        <p class="by display">owns the market.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="measure">
        <p class="label">A CRO</p>
        <p class="by display">owns the revenue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="measure founder">
        <p class="label">A founder</p>
        <p class="by display">owns all of it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pairing">We fill the seat you need, and think like the person who owns all of it.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="ink" label="Start where you are" title="Which sounds like you?">
    <div class="grid-2">
      <Card
        variant="path"
        href="/ecommerce"
        kicker="Ecommerce and consumer brands"
        title="You sell online, on Amazon or into retail."
        cta="For ecommerce brands"
      >
        <p>Sharper customer, stronger offer. Data-led decisions on channels, creative and budget, so you scale what pays.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card
        variant="path"
        href="/startups"
        kicker="B2B, SaaS and service businesses"
        title="You need a CRO, CMO or GTM lead, but not full-time."
        cta="For B2B businesses"
      >
        <p>
          We sharpen who you sell to and how you win them: go-to-market, pipeline, sales process and pricing, with the
          numbers the board needs to see.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream" label="The awkward stage" title="You probably don't need another agency.">
    <div class="problem">
      <div class="lede-col">
        <p class="lede">
          Growing businesses reach an awkward stage. There are people, agencies, software and ideas, yet growth is
          uneven, decisions still route through the founder, and nobody owns the whole commercial picture.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          The problem might be sales, marketing, pricing, ecommerce or how the team is set up. Hire a specialist before
          you know which, and the machine gets more complicated, not better.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="symptoms">
        <Card variant="symptom" title="Growth has stalled, or stopped being predictable.">
          <p>And nobody can say whether it is a revenue problem or a margin problem.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card variant="symptom" title="Every important decision still goes through the founder.">
          <p>So the business can only grow as fast as one person's diary.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card variant="symptom" title="You are about to hire a CRO or a CMO.">
          <p>Before knowing which seat the business actually needs filled.</p>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="ink" id="how-we-work" label="How we work" title="Find the leak, then the lever.">
    <p class="lede">
      The same four stages on every engagement, in the same order. The first is the deep dive. The last is making sure
      the business no longer needs us.
    </p>
    <MachineRun />
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream" id="ways-to-work" label="Ways to work with us" title="One way in. Two ways to continue.">
    <p class="lede">
      Every engagement starts with a paid deep dive. What happens next depends on what it finds, and the decision is
      yours.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <Card
        variant="engagement"
        kicker="Start here"
        title="The Machine Check"
        principle="Everything ranked by what it costs you."
        href="/how-we-work/machine-check"
        cta="About the Machine Check"
      >
        <p>
          A fixed-fee deep dive into the whole commercial picture. You get a ranked view of what each problem costs
          you, in revenue and in margin, with our reasoning and what to do first.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card
        variant="engagement"
        kicker="If the fix is a thing"
        title="The Build"
        principle="It has to still work after we leave."
        href="/how-we-work/build"
        cta="About the Build"
      >
        <p>
          A defined project with a handover: a strategy, a plan, a sales process, a system or an AI tool. We build it
          with your team and leave it running.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card
        variant="engagement"
        kicker="If the fix is leadership"
        title="The Growth Office"
        principle="In the business, not on a call."
        href="/how-we-work/growth-office"
        cta="About the Growth Office"
      >
        <p>
          One or both of us in your business part-time, owning the growth agenda and doing the work alongside your
          people. When you are ready to hire permanently, we help you hire and hand over.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
    <div class="bench">
      <p class="label">Specialists</p>
      <p class="muted">
        We are two. When a job needs a discipline we don't have, we bring in a specialist we have worked with, at their
        rate, and you see the number before we commit it. We don't mark up other people's time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="ink" label="Who you actually get" title="Two senior operators. No juniors, no handoff.">
    <p class="lede">
      The people you meet are the people doing the work. The problem decides who leads, and most clients get both of
      us.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-2 bios">
      <BioBlock
        name="Andrew Price"
        role="Revenue, sales and commercial strategy"
        pending="Andrew's full bio, portrait and three to five career results"
      >
        <p>Multiple-time founder, CEO and chief revenue officer, across B2B and B2C.</p>
      </BioBlock>
      <BioBlock
        name="Tarren Price"
        role="Ecommerce and consumer brands"
        pending="Tarren's full bio, portrait and three to five career results"
      >
        <p>
          Ecommerce and FMCG personal care, across Amazon, Shopify and Meta advertising. Builds and reshapes ecommerce
          operations to lift revenue and margin.
        </p>
      </BioBlock>
    </div>
    <div class="record">
      <h3 class="display h3">Before The Growth Machine.</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        What we have done in our own careers, labelled as exactly that. Client results replace this as soon as there
        are results we are allowed to publish.
      </p>
      <Placeholder needs="Career results from Andrew and Tarren, written as problem, action, result, with numbers only where they can be stood behind" />
    </div>
    <p><a class="link" href="/who-we-are">Meet Andrew and Tarren <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </Section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Not sure whether you need a CRO, a CMO or something else? Good. That is where we start."
    href="/call"
    action="Book a 30-minute call"
    tone="cream"
  >
    There are two of us, so we take on a small number of clients at a time. Thirty minutes, no deck: we will ask where
    you are trying to get to and what is in the way.
  </CtaBand>
</Base>

<style>
  .reframe { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px); align-items: center; }
  .sides { display: grid; gap: 28px; }
  .side { display: grid; gap: 8px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .side p { max-width: 32em; }
  .levers { font-family: var(--f-label); font-size: 0.82rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
  /* the section's point: three ways of keeping score across the full width,
     the founder's marked, so the comparison is seen before it is read */
  .measures { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px; }
  .measure { display: grid; gap: 10px; align-content: start; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .measure.founder { border-top: 3px solid var(--torch); padding-top: 18px; }
  .measure .by { font-size: var(--step-h3); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: var(--track-display); max-width: 10em; }
  .measure:not(.founder) .by { color: var(--muted); }
  .pairing { font-size: var(--step-lede); font-weight: 600; margin-top: -8px; }

  .grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px; }
  .grid-3 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px; }

  .problem { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px); align-items: start; }
  .lede-col { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .lede-col .muted { max-width: 34em; }
  .symptoms { display: grid; gap: 28px; }

  .bench { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 200px) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px 32px; align-items: baseline; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 24px; }
  .bench .muted { max-width: 44em; }

  .bios { gap: 40px; }
  .record { display: grid; gap: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 28px; }
  .record .muted { max-width: 40em; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .grid-3 { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .reframe, .problem, .grid-2, .bench { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .measures { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0; }
    .measure { grid-template-columns: 7.5em minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; padding-block: 14px; }
    .measure.founder { padding-top: 12px; }
  }
</style>
